on, then use the rerun/canary/decontamination budget to isolate the causal knob and write the required JSON."}], "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1790561817.049377, "turn_id": "01a0e5cd-105b-7723-8272-7354daca7c49"}, "phase": "commentary", "role": "assistant", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a0e5cd-105b-7723-8272-7354daca7c49"}}, {"id": "fc_0bfd8725de7d1216016ab9ce35745487d08dc4cfc458d79ed4", "type": "function_call", "arguments": "{\"command\":[\"bash\",\"-lc\",\"/app/bin/lab spec\"],\"timeout_ms\":150000,\"workdir\":\"/app\"}", "call_id": "call_wmBAZYNNoAzraWtSYwcHRhmx", "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1790561817.049377, "turn_id": "01a0e5cd-105b-7723-8272-7354daca7c49"}, "name": "shell", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a0e5cd-105b-7723-8272-7354daca7c49"}}, {"type": "function_call_output", "call_id": "call_wmBAZYNNoAzraWtSYwcHRhmx", "output": "{\"exit_code\": 0, \"duration_s\": 0.0, \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"ops\\\": {\\n  \\\"rerun\\\": {\\n   \\\"args\\\": {\\n    \\\"config\\\": \\\"object with any of ['capacity', 'leak', 'mixture', 'lr_scale']; omitted knobs keep their RELEASE value\\\",\\n    \\\"reps\\\": \\\"independent repeats, 1..3 (default 1)\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"cost\\\": \\\"1 re-run per rep, x1.5-2 when capacity or mixture is changed (retraining)\\\",\\n   \\\"returns\\\": \\\"per repeat: offline_slice, offline_other; plus their means\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"canary\\\": {\\n   \\\"args\\\": {\\n    \\\"config\\\": \\\"object, same shape as rerun\\\",\\n    \\\"reps\\\": \\\"1..3 (default 1)\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"cost\\\": \\\"4 re-runs per rep, x1.5-2 when capacity or mixture is changed\\\",\\n   \\\"returns\\\": \\\"the ONLINE slice number of that config, averaged over the repeats\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"decontaminate\\\": {\\n   \\\"args\\\": {\\n    \\\"config\\\": \\\"object, same shape as rerun\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"cost\\\": \\\"1 re-run\\\",\\n   \\\"returns\\\": \\\"the offline slice number of that config on a decontaminated eval slice\\\"\\n  }\\n },\\n \\\"deliverable\\\": \\\"/app/report.json (see /app/docs/report_format.md)\\\",\\n \\\"budget_total\\\": 20.0,\\n \\\"budget_left\\\": 20.0\\n}\\n\"}"}, {"id": "fc_0bfd8725de7d1216016ab9ce9609bc87d0bb3a9e723a47ac2e", "type": "function_call", "arguments": "{\"command\":[\"bash\",\"-lc\",\"cat /app/docs/report_format.md\"],\"timeout_ms\":150000,\"workdir\":\"/app\"}", "call_id": "call_GhoEBM3suEUUMxQuLwDGTn4r", "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1790561939.958928, "turn_id": "01a0e5ce-ef83-7054-8625-0cea8bf6c118"}, "name": "shell", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a0e5ce-ef83-7054-8625-0cea8bf6c118"}}, {"type": "function_call_output", "call_id": "call_GhoEBM3suEUUMxQuLwDGTn4r", "output": "{\"exit_code\": 0, \"duration_s\": 0.0, \"output\": \"# report.json\\n\\n    {\\n      \\\"cause\\\": \\\"<one of ['capacity', 'mixture', 'lr_scale']>\\\",\\n      \\\"fix\\\": {\\\"<knob>\\\": 0.0,          // the knob you blamed, moved as far as the release note allows\\n              \\\"<other knob>\\\": 0.0}    // and whatever else you had to re-tune around it\\n    }\\n\\nThe values above are placeholders, not a worked example - fill in what you measured.\\n\\nKnobs you leave out keep their **release** value. The grader clamps `fix` to the same release constraint the\\nlab enforces, so asking for a value beyond the cap silently gets you the cap.\\n\"}"}, {"id": "rs_0bfd8725de7d1216016ab9cf8caaa087d0b402a6b8e670284f", "type": "reasoning", "content": [], "encrypted_content": "gAAAAABquc-MWsjlgeVKR1k0-R3XV23TfleyzQiHjlPN2qpVpy2JNJZqu1H-Ne4TXfh3LsWq-rRSSCQADweqDBntKz-RTLpmvJYioI7ZoHByLXN_R_4Y5CikqFAsevGDqmmj0kci3oN1q-yceqPYbC9VLNCczEpJkxHDVG0Ut6-qCBJK63qPw3K6kVxYr84ILU9SE537isgGUDlrpaMk3uUx5Cj1pORMYENOxLYQJfXJCPPBgH1aITntbqIitLcwG2MMOlQQouZx_RPsiTOf6EhW8_1Zb_1VUQHwXiX5YycIECAeS04T6zBJ0JcvdXttFo4Bo3sb-1SCnrGNFFvkQrEsX4GziAqPNskl7ltlhcF_xXmCv2TH3gzSwsqmidxrc9AFmVa_pxd1KWCM907AS_X7I8hct_wKr2gg_zhH-TyOTcWyk9Tg0qOmTBBCKn